    pr_ref:  # a9b9
    description: "When updating tracker items to resolved states (done, holding, etc.), context about WHY the status changed often needs to be recorded. The agent attempted --note on update, which doesn't exist, then retried without it — losing the context (META-radiz: PRs #1450 and #1452 context lost).\n\nProposal: Add guidance to AGENTS.md tracker section:\n- When changing status to a resolved state, ALWAYS follow up with `scripts/tracker discuss <ID> \"reason for status change\"` to record the rationale.\n- Example: after `scripts/tracker update FOO --status holding`, run `scripts/tracker discuss FOO \"Implemented in PR #1234.\"`.\n\nThis is a governance file change (AGENTS.md) and requires human approval."  # a9b9
    fields: {}  # a9b9
